IMPORT prelude

-- Legislation Act 2003 (Commonwealth), Chapter 2 Part 1: the Federal Register of Legislation (sections 15A to 15M).
-- Text: C2004A01224.txt, compilation C2019C00084; it is not the authorised text.
--
-- Shape of the rules in this module.
-- A duty or a power is stated once, as one function named for the provision and the party: it answers whether the duty or power arises on the facts given.
-- JUST TRUE: the text imposes the duty or gives the power on those facts.
-- JUST FALSE: the text itself says no (a flat negative, or a condition worded "if").
-- NOTHING: the facts are outside what the provision speaks of, so the text does not say.
-- A comment line "jural:" above a rule names the holder of the right, privilege, power or immunity and the bearer of the correlative.
-- The days by which a thing must be done, where the text counts them, are computed in lga-time.l4 and are not restated here.
-- The open-textured words ("as soon as practicable", "considers") are not decided here: whether the person considers a thing is a plain input.

§ `Section 15A: the Federal Register of Legislation (establishment and maintenance)`

DECLARE `Document` IS ONE OF
    `an Act as made, registered under this Part`
    `a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument as made, registered under this Part`
    `a compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, registered under this Part`
    `an explanatory statement for a legislative instrument, registered under this Part`
    `another document registered under this Part`
    `an Act as made, other than an Act registered under this Part`
    `an instrument as made, other than a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument registered under this Part`
    `a Gazette notice`
    `a compilation of an Act or instrument, other than a compilation registered under this Part`
    `a document that may be considered under section 15AB of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 in working out the meaning of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`
    `any other document`

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:299 | (1) The First Parliamentary Counsel must establish and maintain a register of Acts, legislative instruments and notifiable instruments, to be known as the Federal Register of Legislation.
@ref s 15A(1) (src:299-299)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15A(1): the First Parliamentary Counsel must establish and maintain the Federal Register of Legislation` MEANS TRUE

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- The Register must contain the five kinds in (2); a document of another kind is not covered by (2), so NOTHING.
-- src:305 | (2) The Register must contain the following:
-- src:306 | (a) Acts as made that are registered under this Part;
-- src:307 | (b) legislative instruments and notifiable instruments as made that are registered under this Part;
-- src:308 | (c) compilations, registered under this Part, of Acts, legislative instruments and notifiable instruments;
-- src:309 | (d) explanatory statements, registered under this Part, for legislative instruments;
-- src:310 | (e) other documents registered under this Part.
@ref s 15A(2) (src:305-310)
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15A(2): the Register must contain the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the document`
    WHEN `an Act as made, registered under this Part` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument as made, registered under this Part` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, registered under this Part` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an explanatory statement for a legislative instrument, registered under this Part` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another document registered under this Part` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an Act as made, other than an Act registered under this Part` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an instrument as made, other than a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument registered under this Part` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a Gazette notice` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a compilation of an Act or instrument, other than a compilation registered under this Part` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a document that may be considered under section 15AB of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 in working out the meaning of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `any other document` THEN NOTHING

-- jural: privilege of the First Parliamentary Counsel | no-right of users of the Register
-- The list in (3) is "including (without limitation)", so a kind not listed is also NOTHING.
-- src:311 | (3) The Register may contain additional documents if the First Parliamentary Counsel considers that the documents are likely to be useful to users of the Register, including the following (without limitation):
-- src:312 | (a) Acts as made (other than Acts registered under this Part);
-- src:313 | (b) instruments as made (other than legislative instruments or notifiable instruments registered under this Part);
-- src:314 | (c) Gazette notices;
-- src:315 | (d) compilations of Acts or instruments (other than compilations registered under this Part);
-- src:316 | (e) documents that may be considered under section 15AB of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (and that section as applied by section 13 of this Act) in working out the meaning of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, for example, an explanatory memorandum for an Act.
@ref s 15A(3) (src:311-316)
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Document`
      `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers that the document is likely to be useful to users of the Register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15A(3): the Register may contain the additional document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the document`
    WHEN `an Act as made, registered under this Part` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument as made, registered under this Part` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, registered under this Part` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an explanatory statement for a legislative instrument, registered under this Part` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `another document registered under this Part` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an Act as made, other than an Act registered under this Part` THEN `useful or not`
    WHEN `an instrument as made, other than a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument registered under this Part` THEN `useful or not`
    WHEN `a Gazette notice` THEN `useful or not`
    WHEN `a compilation of an Act or instrument, other than a compilation registered under this Part` THEN `useful or not`
    WHEN `a document that may be considered under section 15AB of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 in working out the meaning of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN `useful or not`
    WHEN `any other document` THEN `useful or not`
    WHERE
        `useful or not` MEANS
            IF `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers that the document is likely to be useful to users of the Register` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- jural: privilege of the First Parliamentary Counsel | no-right of users of the Register
-- src:317 | (4) The First Parliamentary Counsel may include in the Register any information that he or she considers likely to be useful to users of the Register.
@ref s 15A(4) (src:317-317)
GIVEN `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers the information likely to be useful to users of the Register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15A(4): the Register may include the information` MEANS
    IF `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers the information likely to be useful to users of the Register` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: power of the First Parliamentary Counsel | liability of anyone affected by what is done
-- src:318 | (5) Without limiting subsection (1), the First Parliamentary Counsel may, subject to this Act and the rules, do anything he or she considers necessary or desirable to ensure that the Register is accurate and up-to-date, and contains material likely to be useful to users of the Register.
@ref s 15A(5) (src:318-318)
GIVEN `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers the thing necessary or desirable to ensure that the Register is accurate and up-to-date, and contains material likely to be useful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is contrary to this Act or the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15A(5): the First Parliamentary Counsel may do the thing` MEANS
    IF `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers the thing necessary or desirable to ensure that the Register is accurate and up-to-date, and contains material likely to be useful` AND NOT `the thing is contrary to this Act or the rules`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 15B and 15C: the Register as the record, and the approved website`

-- src:320 | The Federal Register of Legislation is, for all purposes, taken to be a complete and accurate record of all registered Acts, legislative instruments and notifiable instruments.
@ref s 15B (src:320-320)
GIVEN `it is a registered Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15B: the Register is taken to be a complete and accurate record of the law` MEANS
    IF `it is a registered Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: claim of the public | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:323 | The First Parliamentary Counsel must ensure that registered Acts, legislative instruments, notifiable instruments and compilations, and other registered documents, are available to the public on a website (an approved website) prescribed by the rules.
@ref s 15C (src:323-323)
GIVEN `it is a registered Act, legislative instrument, notifiable instrument or compilation, or another registered document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15C: the First Parliamentary Counsel must ensure the material is available to the public on the approved website` MEANS
    IF `it is a registered Act, legislative instrument, notifiable instrument or compilation, or another registered document` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 15D: rectification of the Register`

DECLARE `Error in the Register` IS ONE OF
    `the text of an Act as it appears in the Register is not the text of the Act as assented to`
    `the text of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument as it appears in the Register is not the text as made by the rule-maker`
    `a compilation as it appears in the Register does not represent the state of the law that it purports to represent`
    `the text of another document as it appears in the Register is not the text of the original document`
    `any other error`

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:325 | (1) If:
-- src:326 | (a) the First Parliamentary Counsel becomes aware that the Register contains an error; and
-- src:327 | (b) the error is that:
-- src:328 | (i) for an Act as assented to—the text of the Act as it appears in the Register is not the same as the text of the Act as assented to; or
-- src:329 | (ii) for a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument as made by the rule-maker—the text of the instrument as it appears in the Register is not the same as the text of the instrument as made by the rule-maker; or
-- src:330 | (iii) for a compilation—the compilation as it appears in the Register does not represent the state of the law that it purports to represent; or
-- src:331 | (iv) for any other document on the Register—the text of the document as it appears in the Register is not the same as the text of the original document;
-- src:332 | the First Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for the error in the Register to be rectified as soon as possible.
@ref s 15D(1) (src:325-332)
GIVEN `the First Parliamentary Counsel becomes aware that the Register contains an error` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the error` IS AN `Error in the Register`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15D(1): the First Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for the error to be rectified as soon as possible` MEANS
    IF `the First Parliamentary Counsel becomes aware that the Register contains an error`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the error`
        WHEN `any other error` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `the text of an Act as it appears in the Register is not the text of the Act as assented to` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the text of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument as it appears in the Register is not the text as made by the rule-maker` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a compilation as it appears in the Register does not represent the state of the law that it purports to represent` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the text of another document as it appears in the Register is not the text of the original document` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:334 | (2) The First Parliamentary Counsel must include in the Register a statement that the rectification has been made, and a brief outline of the rectification in general terms.
@ref s 15D(2) (src:334-334)
GIVEN `a rectification has been made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15D(2): the First Parliamentary Counsel must include a statement of the rectification and a brief outline in the Register` MEANS
    IF `a rectification has been made under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: immunity of a person who relied on the Register | disability of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:335 | (3) The rectification:
-- src:336 | (a) does not affect any right or privilege that was acquired, or that accrued, because of reliance on the content of the Register before the rectification was made; and
-- src:337 | (b) does not impose or increase any obligation or liability that was incurred before the rectification was made.
@ref s 15D(3) (src:335-337)
GIVEN `the right or privilege was acquired, or accrued, because of reliance on the content of the Register before the rectification was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15D(3)(a): the rectification affects the right or privilege` MEANS
    IF `the right or privilege was acquired, or accrued, because of reliance on the content of the Register before the rectification was made` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 15D(3)(b) (src:337-337)
GIVEN `the obligation or liability was incurred before the rectification was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15D(3)(b): the rectification imposes or increases the obligation or liability` MEANS
    IF `the obligation or liability was incurred before the rectification was made` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:338 | Rectification does not affect time of registration
-- src:339 | (4) To avoid doubt, the rectification of an error under subsection (1) in relation to an instrument does not affect the time at which the instrument is taken to have been registered.
-- src:340 | Note: For example, subsection (1) does not affect the commencement of an instrument that is expressed to commence on the day after registration.
@ref s 15D(4) (src:338-340)
GIVEN `it is the rectification of an error under subsection (1) in relation to an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15D(4): the rectification affects the time at which the instrument is taken to have been registered` MEANS
    IF `it is the rectification of an error under subsection (1) in relation to an instrument` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 15DA: re-tabling and a new disallowance period after rectification`

DECLARE `Facts for section 15DA` HAS
    `the First Parliamentary Counsel rectifies an error referred to in subparagraph 15D(1)(b)(ii)`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rectification results in the originally tabled version of a disallowable legislative instrument being replaced by the correct version` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at the time of the rectification the originally tabled version has been laid before either or both Houses under subsection 38(1)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the instrument has been disallowed at the time it is delivered to a House under subsection (2)`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the disallowance period for the originally tabled version has ended`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:342 | (1) This section applies if:
-- src:343 | (a) the First Parliamentary Counsel rectifies an error in the Register referred to in subparagraph 15D(1)(b)(ii); and
-- src:344 | (b) the rectification results in a version (the originally tabled version) of a disallowable legislative instrument that was previously registered being replaced by another version (the correct version) of the instrument; and
-- src:345 | (c) at the time of the rectification, the originally tabled version of the instrument has been laid before either or both Houses of the Parliament under subsection 38(1).
@ref s 15DA(1) (src:342-345)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for section 15DA`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15DA(1): this section applies` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `the First Parliamentary Counsel rectifies an error referred to in subparagraph 15D(1)(b)(ii)`
    AND `the facts`'s `the rectification results in the originally tabled version of a disallowable legislative instrument being replaced by the correct version`
    AND `the facts`'s `at the time of the rectification the originally tabled version has been laid before either or both Houses under subsection 38(1)`

-- The days are counted in lga-time.l4 (s 15DA(2)).
-- jural: claim of each House | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:347 | (2) The First Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy of the correct version of the instrument to be delivered to each House of the Parliament to be laid before each House within 6 sitting days of that House after the rectification.
@ref s 15DA(2) (src:347-347)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for section 15DA`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15DA(2): the First Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for the correct version to be delivered to each House to be laid` MEANS
    IF `s 15DA(1): this section applies` `the facts` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (3) applies "subject to subsection (4)": it does not apply to an instrument that has been disallowed when it is delivered.
-- src:350 | (3) The following applies (subject to subsection (4)) for the purposes of this Act:
-- src:351 | (a) the instrument is taken to have been delivered to, and laid before, a House of the Parliament under subsection 38(1) when the instrument is delivered to, and laid before, that House under subsection (2) of this section (except for the purposes of subsection 39(2));
-- src:352 | (b) the instrument becomes subject to disallowance under Part 2 of Chapter 3;
-- src:353 | (c) section 46 applies as if the instrument had been registered at the time of the rectification;
-- src:354 | (d) if the disallowance period for the originally tabled version has ended—any repeal of the instrument or a provision of the instrument under section 48A or 48C is taken not to have occurred;
-- src:355 | (e) if:
-- src:356 | (i) a notice of motion to disallow the instrument or a provision of the instrument has been given in a House of the Parliament; and
-- src:357 | (ii) the notice has not been withdrawn; and
-- src:358 | (iii) the motion has not been disposed of;
-- src:359 | at the time the correct version of the instrument is laid before a House as mentioned in subsection (2)—that notice of motion is taken to have been given in that House on the sitting day of that House after the correct version of the instrument is laid before that House;
-- src:360 | (f) if a provision of the instrument (but not the whole instrument) has previously been disallowed—the laying before a House of the Parliament as mentioned in subsection (2) does not affect the previous disallowance of the provision.
@ref s 15DA(3) (src:350-360)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for section 15DA`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15DA(3): the effects listed in subsection (3) apply` MEANS
    `s 15DA(1): this section applies` `the facts`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the instrument has been disallowed at the time it is delivered to a House under subsection (2)`

@ref s 15DA(3)(a) (src:351-351)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for section 15DA`
      `the purpose is section 39(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15DA(3)(a): the instrument is taken to have been delivered to and laid before the House under subsection 38(1) when it is laid under subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `s 15DA(3): the effects listed in subsection (3) apply` `the facts`
    THEN (IF `the purpose is section 39(2)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 15DA(3)(b) (src:352-352)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for section 15DA`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15DA(3)(b): the instrument becomes subject to disallowance under Part 2 of Chapter 3` MEANS
    IF `s 15DA(3): the effects listed in subsection (3) apply` `the facts` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 15DA(3)(c) (src:353-353)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for section 15DA`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15DA(3)(c): section 46 applies as if the instrument had been registered at the time of the rectification` MEANS
    IF `s 15DA(3): the effects listed in subsection (3) apply` `the facts` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 15DA(3)(d) (src:354-354)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for section 15DA`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15DA(3)(d): a repeal of the instrument or a provision under section 48A or 48C is taken not to have occurred` MEANS
    IF `s 15DA(3): the effects listed in subsection (3) apply` `the facts`
    THEN (IF `the facts`'s `the disallowance period for the originally tabled version has ended` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 15DA(3)(e) (src:355-359)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for section 15DA`
      `a notice of motion to disallow has been given in a House` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice has not been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the motion has not been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15DA(3)(e): the notice of motion is taken to have been given on the sitting day after the correct version is laid` MEANS
    IF `s 15DA(3): the effects listed in subsection (3) apply` `the facts`
    THEN (IF `a notice of motion to disallow has been given in a House` AND `the notice has not been withdrawn` AND `the motion has not been disposed of` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 15DA(3)(f) (src:360-360)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for section 15DA`
      `a provision of the instrument but not the whole instrument has previously been disallowed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15DA(3)(f): the laying before a House affects the previous disallowance of the provision` MEANS
    IF `s 15DA(3): the effects listed in subsection (3) apply` `the facts`
    THEN (IF `a provision of the instrument but not the whole instrument has previously been disallowed` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:361 | (4) Subsection (3) does not apply in relation to an instrument if, at the time the instrument is delivered to a House of the Parliament under subsection (2), the instrument has been disallowed.
@ref s 15DA(4) (src:361-361)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for section 15DA`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15DA(4): subsection (3) does not apply to the instrument` MEANS
    `the facts`'s `the instrument has been disallowed at the time it is delivered to a House under subsection (2)`

-- src:363 | (5) To avoid doubt, the laying before a House of the Parliament of an instrument as mentioned in subsection (2) does not affect the time at which the instrument is taken to have been registered (except as provided by paragraph (3)(c)).
@ref s 15DA(5) (src:363-363)
GIVEN `the laying is as mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the effect given by paragraph (3)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15DA(5): the laying before a House affects the time at which the instrument is taken to have been registered` MEANS
    IF `the laying is as mentioned in subsection (2)`
    THEN (IF `it is the effect given by paragraph (3)(c)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 15F to 15H: registering, lodging and withdrawing`

-- jural: claim of nobody the text names | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:373 | The First Parliamentary Counsel must register an Act as soon as practicable after the Act is assented to.
@ref s 15F (src:373-373)
GIVEN `the Act has been assented to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15F: the First Parliamentary Counsel must register the Act as soon as practicable after assent` MEANS
    IF `the Act has been assented to` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: claim of the First Parliamentary Counsel | duty of the rule-maker
-- src:376 | (1) The rule-maker for a legislative instrument must lodge the instrument for registration as a legislative instrument as soon as practicable after the instrument is made.
@ref s 15G(1) (src:376-376)
GIVEN `the instrument has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15G(1): the rule-maker must lodge the instrument for registration as a legislative instrument as soon as practicable after it is made` MEANS
    IF `it is a legislative instrument` AND `the instrument has been made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: claim of the First Parliamentary Counsel | duty of the rule-maker
-- src:377 | (2) The rule-maker for a notifiable instrument must lodge the instrument for registration as a notifiable instrument as soon as practicable after the instrument is made.
@ref s 15G(2) (src:377-377)
GIVEN `the instrument has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15G(2): the rule-maker must lodge the instrument for registration as a notifiable instrument as soon as practicable after it is made` MEANS
    IF `it is a notifiable instrument` AND `the instrument has been made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: privilege of the rule-maker | no-right of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:378 | (3) The rule-maker for an instrument made under a power delegated by the Parliament, other than a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, may lodge the instrument for registration as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument.
@ref s 15G(3) (src:378-378)
GIVEN `it is an instrument made under a power delegated by the Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15G(3): the rule-maker may lodge the instrument for registration as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is an instrument made under a power delegated by the Parliament` AND NOT (`it is a legislative instrument` OR `it is a notifiable instrument`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Explanatory statement` IS ONE OF
    `an initial explanatory statement`
    `a supplementary explanatory statement`
    `a replacement explanatory statement`

-- jural: claim of the First Parliamentary Counsel | duty of the rule-maker
-- src:381 | (4) The rule-maker for an instrument that is lodged for registration as a legislative instrument must:
-- src:382 | (a) lodge an initial explanatory statement for the instrument for registration as soon as practicable after the instrument is lodged for registration; and
-- src:383 | (b) lodge any supplementary explanatory statement or replacement explanatory statement for the instrument for registration as soon as practicable after it is prepared.
@ref s 15G(4) (src:381-383)
GIVEN `the instrument is lodged for registration as a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement` IS AN `Explanatory statement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15G(4): the rule-maker must lodge the explanatory statement for registration as soon as practicable` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is lodged for registration as a legislative instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: privilege of the rule-maker | no-right of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:386 | (5) The rule-maker for an instrument that is, or that is to be, registered as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument may lodge a document that relates to the instrument for registration.
@ref s 15G(5) (src:386-386)
GIVEN `the instrument is, or is to be, registered as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document relates to the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15G(5): the rule-maker may lodge the document for registration` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is, or is to be, registered as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` AND `the document relates to the instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `How lodged` IS ONE OF
    `lodged for registration as a legislative instrument`
    `lodged for registration as a notifiable instrument`
    `lodged for registration otherwise than as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`

-- jural: claim of the rule-maker | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:388 | (1) If an instrument is lodged for registration as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument in accordance with section 15G and the rules, the First Parliamentary Counsel must register the instrument:
-- src:389 | (a) if the instrument is lodged for registration as a legislative instrument—as a legislative instrument; or
-- src:390 | (b) if the instrument is lodged for registration as a notifiable instrument—as a notifiable instrument.
@ref s 15H(1) (src:388-390)
GIVEN `the instrument is lodged in accordance with section 15G and the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how it is lodged` IS A `How lodged`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15H(1): the First Parliamentary Counsel must register the instrument as lodged` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is lodged in accordance with section 15G and the rules`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `how it is lodged`
        WHEN `lodged for registration as a legislative instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `lodged for registration as a notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `lodged for registration otherwise than as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: claim of the person lodging | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:391 | (2) If an instrument or document is lodged for registration otherwise than as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, in accordance with section 15G and the rules, the First Parliamentary Counsel must register the instrument or document accordingly.
@ref s 15H(2) (src:391-391)
GIVEN `the instrument or document is lodged in accordance with section 15G and the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how it is lodged` IS A `How lodged`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15H(2): the First Parliamentary Counsel must register the instrument or document accordingly` MEANS
    IF `the instrument or document is lodged in accordance with section 15G and the rules`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `how it is lodged`
        WHEN `lodged for registration otherwise than as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `lodged for registration as a legislative instrument` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `lodged for registration as a notifiable instrument` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: immunity of the person lodging | disability of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:392 | (3) However, the First Parliamentary Counsel must not register an instrument or document if:
-- src:393 | (a) for a document lodged for registration otherwise than as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument—the First Parliamentary Counsel considers that:
-- src:394 | (i) the document is not likely to be useful to users of the Register; or
-- src:395 | (ii) it would otherwise be inappropriate to register the document; or
-- src:396 | (b) before the instrument or document is registered, the person lodging the instrument or document (or another person acting on behalf of the responsible person for the instrument, or for the instrument to which the document relates) withdraws the lodgement.
@ref s 15H(3) (src:392-396)
GIVEN `how it is lodged` IS A `How lodged`
      `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers that the document is not likely to be useful to users of the Register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers that it would otherwise be inappropriate to register the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before registration the lodgement is withdrawn by the person lodging, or by another person acting on behalf of the responsible person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15H(3): the First Parliamentary Counsel must not register the instrument or document` MEANS
    IF `before registration the lodgement is withdrawn by the person lodging, or by another person acting on behalf of the responsible person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        CONSIDER `how it is lodged`
        WHEN `lodged for registration otherwise than as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN
            (IF `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers that the document is not likely to be useful to users of the Register` OR `the First Parliamentary Counsel considers that it would otherwise be inappropriate to register the document` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)
        WHEN `lodged for registration as a legislative instrument` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `lodged for registration as a notifiable instrument` THEN NOTHING

-- jural: claim of the person lodging | duty of the First Parliamentary Counsel
-- src:397 | (4) If the First Parliamentary Counsel does not register an instrument or document because of paragraph (3)(a), he or she must give written notice to the person lodging the instrument or document.
@ref s 15H(4) (src:397-397)
GIVEN `the First Parliamentary Counsel did not register the instrument or document because of paragraph (3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15H(4): the First Parliamentary Counsel must give written notice to the person lodging` MEANS
    IF `the First Parliamentary Counsel did not register the instrument or document because of paragraph (3)(a)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 15J: explanatory statements`

DECLARE `Facts about a statement for section 15J(1)` HAS
    `it is prepared for laying before each House of the Parliament`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `it complies with subsection (2)`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `it replaces an explanatory statement for the instrument that has already been registered`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `it amends an initial explanatory statement or a replacement explanatory statement`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `it complies with subsection (3)`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN

-- A statement is an explanatory statement for a legislative instrument if it is "one of the following": a closed list, so another statement is JUST FALSE.
-- src:400 | (1) An explanatory statement for a legislative instrument is one of the following statements prepared for laying before each House of Parliament:
-- src:401 | (a) a statement (an initial explanatory statement) for the instrument that complies with subsection (2);
-- src:402 | (b) a statement (a replacement explanatory statement) for the instrument that:
-- src:403 | (i) replaces an explanatory statement for the instrument that has already been registered; and
-- src:404 | (ii) complies with subsection (2);
-- src:405 | (c) a statement (a supplementary explanatory statement) for the instrument that:
-- src:406 | (i) amends an initial explanatory statement or a replacement explanatory statement; and
-- src:407 | (ii) complies with subsection (3).
@ref s 15J(1) (src:400-407)
GIVEN `the kind` IS AN `Explanatory statement`
      `the facts` IS A `Facts about a statement for section 15J(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15J(1): the statement is an explanatory statement for a legislative instrument` MEANS
    IF `the facts`'s `it is prepared for laying before each House of the Parliament`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `an initial explanatory statement` THEN `the facts`'s `it complies with subsection (2)`
        WHEN `a replacement explanatory statement` THEN
                `the facts`'s `it replaces an explanatory statement for the instrument that has already been registered`
            AND `the facts`'s `it complies with subsection (2)`
        WHEN `a supplementary explanatory statement` THEN
                `the facts`'s `it amends an initial explanatory statement or a replacement explanatory statement`
            AND `the facts`'s `it complies with subsection (3)`
    ELSE FALSE

DECLARE `Facts about an initial or replacement explanatory statement` HAS
    `it is approved by the rule-maker`                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it explains the purpose and operation of the instrument`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `documents are incorporated in the instrument by reference`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contains a description of the incorporated documents and indicates how they may be obtained`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `consultation was undertaken under section 17 before the instrument was made`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contains a description of the nature of that consultation`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `it explains why no such consultation was undertaken`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the instrument is a disallowable legislative instrument`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contains a statement of compatibility prepared under subsection 9(1) of the Human Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contains such other information as is prescribed by regulation`                                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- The requirements are cumulative: each paragraph that applies must be met.
-- src:409 | (2) An initial explanatory statement, or a replacement explanatory statement, for a legislative instrument must:
-- src:410 | (a) be approved by the rule-maker; and
-- src:411 | (b) explain the purpose and operation of the instrument; and
-- src:412 | (c) if any documents are incorporated in the instrument by reference—contain a description of the incorporated documents and indicate how they may be obtained; and
-- src:413 | (d) if consultation was undertaken under section 17 before the instrument was made—contain a description of the nature of that consultation; and
-- src:414 | (e) if no such consultation was undertaken—explain why no such consultation was undertaken; and
-- src:415 | (f) if the instrument is a disallowable legislative instrument—contain a statement of compatibility prepared under subsection 9(1) of the Human Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011; and
-- src:416 | (g) contain such other information as is prescribed by regulation.
@ref s 15J(2) (src:409-416)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an initial or replacement explanatory statement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15J(2): the statement meets the requirements for an initial or replacement explanatory statement` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `it is approved by the rule-maker`
    AND `the facts`'s `it explains the purpose and operation of the instrument`
    AND (`the facts`'s `documents are incorporated in the instrument by reference` IMPLIES `the facts`'s `it contains a description of the incorporated documents and indicates how they may be obtained`)
    AND (`the facts`'s `consultation was undertaken under section 17 before the instrument was made` IMPLIES `the facts`'s `it contains a description of the nature of that consultation`)
    AND ((NOT `the facts`'s `consultation was undertaken under section 17 before the instrument was made`) IMPLIES `the facts`'s `it explains why no such consultation was undertaken`)
    AND (`the facts`'s `the instrument is a disallowable legislative instrument` IMPLIES `the facts`'s `it contains a statement of compatibility prepared under subsection 9(1) of the Human Rights (Parliamentary Scrutiny) Act 2011`)
    AND `the facts`'s `it contains such other information as is prescribed by regulation`

-- src:418 | (3) A supplementary explanatory statement for a legislative instrument must:
-- src:419 | (a) be approved by the rule-maker; and
-- src:420 | (b) contain such other information as is prescribed by regulation.
@ref s 15J(3) (src:418-420)
GIVEN `it is approved by the rule-maker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains such other information as is prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15J(3): the statement meets the requirements for a supplementary explanatory statement` MEANS
    `it is approved by the rule-maker` AND `it contains such other information as is prescribed by regulation`

-- jural: privilege of the rule-maker | no-right of anyone to insist on one statement for each instrument
-- src:422 | (4) A single explanatory statement may relate to one or more legislative instruments.
@ref s 15J(4) (src:422-422)
GIVEN `the number of legislative instruments the statement relates to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15J(4): a single explanatory statement may relate to those legislative instruments` MEANS
    IF `the number of legislative instruments the statement relates to` AT LEAST 1 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 15K: enforceability`

-- A legislative instrument "is not enforceable ... unless" registered: unregistered answers JUST FALSE; registered, the section does not say it is enforceable, so NOTHING.
-- jural: immunity of any person (including the Commonwealth) | disability of anyone who would enforce an unregistered instrument
-- src:424 | (1) A legislative instrument is not enforceable by or against any person (including the Commonwealth) unless the instrument is registered as a legislative instrument.
@ref s 15K(1) (src:424-424)
GIVEN `the instrument is registered as a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15K(1): the legislative instrument is enforceable by or against any person (including the Commonwealth)` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is registered as a legislative instrument` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:425 | (2) A failure by the rule-maker to lodge an explanatory statement in relation to a legislative instrument for registration as required by subsection 15G(4) does not affect the validity or enforceability of the instrument.
@ref s 15K(2) (src:425-425)
GIVEN `the rule-maker failed to lodge an explanatory statement for registration as required by subsection 15G(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15K(2): the failure to lodge an explanatory statement affects the validity or enforceability of the instrument` MEANS
    IF `the rule-maker failed to lodge an explanatory statement for registration as required by subsection 15G(4)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 15L: notice of events affecting the Register`

DECLARE `Event affecting the Register` IS ONE OF
    `an event resulting in, or otherwise affecting, the commencement of the Act or instrument (or a provision of it)`
    `the occurrence of a day or time specified in the Act or instrument, or the making of a commencement instrument, resulting in or affecting commencement`
    `a discretionary compilation event`
    `a required compilation event`
    `an event resulting in the Act or instrument (or a provision of it) being repealed, lapsing, expiring or otherwise ceasing to be in force`
    `an event resulting in the Act or instrument, or a provision of it, being (or being declared by a court or tribunal to be) invalid or unenforceable`
    `the responsible person's becoming aware of an error in the Register to which subsection 15D(1) may apply`
    `the responsible person's becoming aware of any other error in the Register`
    `another event prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph (1)(f)`
    `for a disallowable legislative instrument, the disallowance of the instrument or a provision of it`
    `for a disallowable legislative instrument, the disallowance of another legislative instrument (or a provision of one) that amends the instrument`
    `the amendment or repeal of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument by the operation of Part 3 of Chapter 3`
    `the amendment or repeal of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument by the operation of Part 4 of Chapter 3`
    `another event prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph (2)(e)`
    `any other event`

-- jural: claim of the First Parliamentary Counsel | duty of the responsible person
-- Subsection (2) says "subsection (1) does not require" notice of its events, so those answer JUST FALSE.
-- src:427 | (1) The responsible person for a registered Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the occurrence of any of the following events in relation to the Act or instrument:
-- src:428 | (a) an event resulting in, or otherwise affecting, the commencement of the Act or instrument (or a provision of the Act or instrument);
-- src:429 | (b) a discretionary compilation event for the Act or instrument;
-- src:430 | (c) an event resulting in the Act or instrument (or a provision of the Act or instrument) being repealed, lapsing, expiring or otherwise ceasing to be in force;
-- src:431 | (d) an event resulting in the Act or instrument, or a provision of the Act or instrument, being (or being declared by a court or tribunal to be) invalid or unenforceable;
-- src:432 | (e) the responsible person’s becoming aware of:
-- src:433 | (i) an error in the Register to which subsection 15D(1) (Federal Register of Legislation—rectification of Register) may apply; or
-- src:434 | (ii) any other error in the Register;
-- src:435 | (f) another event prescribed by the rules.
-- src:436 | Example: If a registered legislative instrument is expressed to commence when a particular treaty comes into force for Australia, paragraph (1)(a) would require the responsible person for the instrument to notify the First Parliamentary Counsel when the treaty comes into force.
-- src:437 | (2) However, subsection (1) does not require the responsible person to give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of any of the following events in relation to a registered Act or instrument:
-- src:438 | (a) the occurrence of a day or time specified in the Act or instrument, or the making of a commencement instrument, resulting in, or otherwise affecting, the commencement of the Act or instrument (or a provision of the Act or instrument);
-- src:439 | (b) a required compilation event for the Act or instrument;
-- src:440 | (c) for a disallowable legislative instrument—the disallowance of:
-- src:441 | (i) the instrument (or a provision of the instrument); or
-- src:442 | (ii) another legislative instrument (or a provision of another legislative instrument) that amends the instrument;
-- src:443 | (d) for a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument—the amendment or repeal of the instrument by:
-- src:444 | (i) the operation of Part 3 of Chapter 3 (repeal of spent instruments or provisions); or
-- src:445 | (ii) the operation of Part 4 of Chapter 3 (sunsetting of legislative instruments);
-- src:446 | (e) another event prescribed by the rules.
@ref s 15L(1) and (2) (src:427-446)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the event` IS AN `Event affecting the Register`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15L: the responsible person must give notice to the First Parliamentary Counsel of the event` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument is registered`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the event`
        WHEN `an event resulting in, or otherwise affecting, the commencement of the Act or instrument (or a provision of it)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a discretionary compilation event` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `an event resulting in the Act or instrument (or a provision of it) being repealed, lapsing, expiring or otherwise ceasing to be in force` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `an event resulting in the Act or instrument, or a provision of it, being (or being declared by a court or tribunal to be) invalid or unenforceable` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the responsible person's becoming aware of an error in the Register to which subsection 15D(1) may apply` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the responsible person's becoming aware of any other error in the Register` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `another event prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph (1)(f)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the occurrence of a day or time specified in the Act or instrument, or the making of a commencement instrument, resulting in or affecting commencement` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `a required compilation event` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `for a disallowable legislative instrument, the disallowance of the instrument or a provision of it` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `for a disallowable legislative instrument, the disallowance of another legislative instrument (or a provision of one) that amends the instrument` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `the amendment or repeal of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument by the operation of Part 3 of Chapter 3` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `the amendment or repeal of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument by the operation of Part 4 of Chapter 3` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `another event prescribed by the rules for the purposes of paragraph (2)(e)` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `any other event` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING
